[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station in a very responsive, natural and mostly upland catchment. GENERAL: Velocity area station; approx. 15m wide. STATION HYDROMETRY: Rock/boulder control (may be subject to erosion/accretion) plus a thin-plate weir in the mill lade (Langholm B, local no. 140, station level 84.17mOD; closed 1990). Combined flows are archived. Peak flow ratings derived from current meter gaugings up to 1.93m (about 0.5 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond. FLOW RECORD: Flows from Jan 2002 reprocessed in 2012. Icing evident in hydrograph 1-14/1/2011. FLOW REGIME: Very responsive, natural catchment (open cast mines and minor effluent discharge close to the station).
CATCHMENT,A mostly upland catchment developed, mainly, on Carboniferous sediments (chiefly Coal Measures) and igneous formations; extensively overlain by superficial deposits. Hill grazing is the major landuse with some forestry. No significant catchment changes known.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to near QMED.
Pooling Suitability,No confidence in estimates for higher flows due to extent of extrapolation above highest gauging and lack of containment in channel.
[END]
